 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Polarity",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "A-suffix parts are unidirectional and carry a cathode band; CA-suffix parts are bidirectional, unbanded, and share the figures of the matching A part, except that at VR of 10 V or below their IR limit doubles. Forward voltage and forward surge ratings (Fig. 6) belong to unidirectional parts only."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulse rating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The 200 W rating is for one 10/1000 µs pulse: a 10 µs rise to peak, then a decay to half the peak at 1 ms (Fig. 3). Each part's VC is its maximum at its own IPP in that pulse. Shorter pulses take more power and longer pulses less: about 8 kW at 1 µs, falling to 0.1 kW near 5 ms (Fig. 1)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Peak pulse power and current hold at 100 % to Ta = 25 ℃ and fall in a straight line to zero at 150 ℃ (Fig. 2). Steady dissipation PM(AV) holds at 0.4 W to 75 ℃ and falls in a straight line to zero at 150 ℃ (Fig. 5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Forward surge",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "From TJ max, a unidirectional part's allowed 8.3 ms half-sine surge falls with the number of 60 Hz cycles, from 20 A at one cycle to about 6 A at 100 cycles (Fig. 6); the ratings table gives IFSM as 30 A."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Leakage and capacitance",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Typical IR is under 5 µA for parts above 12 V; the table maximum is 1 µA from SMF13A up, 2.5 µA for SMF10A to SMF12A, and up to 500 µA at the lowest voltage. Zero-bias junction capacitance falls with breakdown voltage: about 2000 pF (uni) and 1160 pF (bi) at 5 V, down to about 30 pF and 18 pF near 430 V (Fig. 4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and failure",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Glass-passivated junction; molding compound rated UL 94V-0; matte tin, lead-free plating; halogen free and RoHS compliant. Terminals withstand 260 ℃ for 40 s during soldering. Whisker testing follows JEDEC JESD201A tables 4a and 4c. ESD per IEC 61000-4-2 is 30 kV air and 30 kV contact. Excess voltage or current typically leaves the part shorted."
  }
 ],
